{"changes":["eka-core/exchange/builder.go: `toUnit` projects `Provenance` from the loaded artifact (`loadedArtifact` embeds `conformance.Artifact`, so the value was already there). The human default is normalised to empty rather than spelled, because the Markdown adapter leaves provenance empty while the JSON adapter fills in `human` for the same undeclared claim — carrying the spelling would make a Markdown export differ in bytes from the JSON re-import of itself, for a distinction the format cannot express.","eka-core/exchange/integrate.go: `artifactProvenance` is the single decision point, used by both renderers (`buildFrontmatter` for the Markdown adapter and `buildJSONAuthoring` for the JSON adapter) instead of duplicated per renderer. It emits nothing for empty or `human`, emits `inferred`/`reconciled`, and refuses any value outside the enum before a byte is written — the Markdown adapter reads no provenance, so an invalid value written there would be lost with no finding.","eka-core/exchange/integrate.go: `frontmatter` and `jsonAuthoring` gained the provenance field, placed to keep the declaration-order serialization contract intact.","eka-core/exchange/artifact_roundtrip_test.go: the doc comment that called the artifact -\u003e unit direction a known gap was corrected; it now names the capture fields that are still not projected (`sourcePromptHash`, `confidence`, `sourceCommitSha`, `captureMeta`), which is the rest of the ADR-035 envelope and a separate decision. No test body changed."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Made provenance survive the package envelope, so export and import agree on how knowledge was obtained instead of resetting every unit to the human default. Owner chose the exchange unit as authoritative for provenance during transport, with the round-trip comparison normalised only where the format genuinely cannot distinguish two states; it turned out no test normalisation was needed at all, because putting the default-to-absence normalisation at the read boundary keeps `TestImportRoundTrip` byte-strict.","tests":["eka-core exchange/provenance_test.go: `TestImportRoundTripCarriesProvenance` (subtests `inferred`, `reconciled`) — export -\u003e import into a fresh repo -\u003e re-export is byte-identical, the exported unit carries the value, and the imported artifact carries the declaration.","eka-core exchange/provenance_test.go: `TestImportRoundTripInventsNoProvenance` — an artifact that declared nothing gains no field and the cycle stays byte-identical.","eka-core exchange/provenance_test.go: `TestBuildFrontmatterProvenance` — the render-level boundary: `\"\"`/`human` emit nothing, `inferred`/`reconciled` emit, out-of-enum refused.","Non-vacuous proof: with only the write side reverted, the round trip reports `entry integrity.json differs between the original and the re-exported package` plus differing package digests; with only `toUnit` reverted, the exported unit is shown missing `\"provenance\":\"inferred\"`.","go test ./exchange/ -count=1 -\u003e ok. go test ./... -count=1 -\u003e all 13 packages ok. gofmt -l exchange/ empty, go vet ./exchange/ clean. `TestImportRoundTrip` and its per-entry diff diagnostics are untouched."]}